WEBVTT

1
00:02:54.894 --> 00:02:56.612
Goddamn bugs.

2
00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:17.452
Oh, shit!

3
00:03:22.094 --> 00:03:23.573
Oh, crap.

4
00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:37.564
Well, Nick the Dick.
What a surprise.

5
00:03:37.814 --> 00:03:39.213
Where you coming from?

6
00:03:39.894 --> 00:03:41.691
Fishing in Cuernavaca.

7
00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:44.129
Sure. Let's take a look
at your catch.

8
00:03:45.414 --> 00:03:46.529
Come on.

9
00:03:53.814 --> 00:03:55.486
I would've thrown them back.

10
00:04:01.814 --> 00:04:04.374
What do you get?
100 bucks a head? 200?

11
00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:08.044
Hope you saved it all for your lawyer.
You'll need it.

12
00:04:12.694 --> 00:04:13.729
We'll take it from here.

13
00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:15.289
Who the hell are you?

14
00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:16.762
INS, Division 6.

15
00:04:17.014 --> 00:04:19.244
Division 6?
I never heard of Division 6.

16
00:04:19.494 --> 00:04:20.483
Really?

17
00:04:21.454 --> 00:04:22.523
Who you betting on?

18
00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:24.608
Tough call, Kay.

19
00:04:25.774 --> 00:04:27.924
What's up, how are you?

20
00:04:28.174 --> 00:04:29.573
Good, good.

21
00:04:30.374 --> 00:04:32.205
Grandma, don't worry.

22
00:04:32.454 --> 00:04:34.763
Welcome to the United States.

23
00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.444
Where are you going, Nogales?

24
00:04:37.814 --> 00:04:39.406
Looking for work?

25
00:04:39.854 --> 00:04:41.287
And you, the same?

26
00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.933
And you?

27
00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.813
Pleasure seeing you here.

28
00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:46.847
And you?

29
00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.168
What if I break your face?

30
00:04:52.454 --> 00:04:54.604
You're very ugly, no?

31
00:04:56.454 --> 00:04:58.365
You don't speak a word of Spanish.

32
00:04:59.654 --> 00:05:00.882
We've got a winner here.

33
00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.487
Oh, I know.

34
00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.004
The rest of you can leave.

35
00:05:05.254 --> 00:05:06.687
Don't move!

36
00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.925
Get in the truck and leave.

37
00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:10.130
Sir, you can't...

38
00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:11.847
Don't "sir" me, young man.

39
00:05:12.054 --> 00:05:14.727
You have no idea
who you're dealing with.

40
00:05:16.374 --> 00:05:19.093
Get in the truck right now!

41
00:05:20.494 --> 00:05:22.803
We'll chat with our friend.
You hit the road.

42
00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:27.724
Keep on protecting us from
the dangerous aliens.

43
00:05:31.894 --> 00:05:33.725
You ever hear of Division 6?

44
00:05:33.974 --> 00:05:35.646
There is no Division 6.

45
00:05:35.894 --> 00:05:36.929
This is bullshit.

46
00:05:37.174 --> 00:05:38.243
Hell, yeah.

47
00:05:39.654 --> 00:05:42.691
Looks like you fell off the bus
in the wrong part of town.

48
00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:45.653
I'll bet you're not
from anywhere near here.

49
00:05:49.454 --> 00:05:50.728
Mikey?

50
00:05:57.694 --> 00:05:59.650
Mikey, when they let you out of jail?

51
00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:02.249
Political refugee.

52
00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:05.247
You know how many treaties
you just violated?

53
00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:07.652
- One?
- Try seven.

54
00:06:10.574 --> 00:06:12.166
You hand me that head.

55
00:06:17.614 --> 00:06:19.093
Put up your arms and flippers.

56
00:06:30.574 --> 00:06:31.450
Shit!

57
00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:37.053
Shoot him!

58
00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:08.013
- "That."
- That...

59
00:07:10.374 --> 00:07:13.764
Was not human. I know.
You got some entrails on you.

60
00:07:15.054 --> 00:07:15.964
What the hell?

61
00:07:16.214 --> 00:07:17.647
The situation's under control.

62
00:07:17.934 --> 00:07:19.970
Give me your attention for a moment.

63
00:07:20.454 --> 00:07:22.046
I'll tell you what happened.

64
00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:34.925
This is called a neuralizer. It's
a gift from friends from out of town.

65
00:07:35.174 --> 00:07:36.926
This red eye isolates...

66
00:07:37.174 --> 00:07:40.086
...the brain's impulses,
specifically the ones for memory.

67
00:07:40.654 --> 00:07:42.770
Give me a splay burn on
the perimeter...

68
00:07:43.014 --> 00:07:45.084
...with holes at 40, 60,
and 80 metres...

69
00:07:45.454 --> 00:07:47.365
...from right here.
Thank you.

70
00:07:52.854 --> 00:07:53.650
That's good.

71
00:07:54.374 --> 00:07:55.568
What's going on?

72
00:07:55.854 --> 00:07:57.207
Excellent question.

73
00:07:57.454 --> 00:07:59.968
The answer you're looking for
lies right here.

74
00:08:02.934 --> 00:08:04.686
Who are you, really?

75
00:08:04.934 --> 00:08:05.730
Really?

76
00:08:06.774 --> 00:08:09.766
I am just a figment
of your imagination.

77
00:08:13.894 --> 00:08:15.850
Damn, what a gullible breed.

78
00:08:17.014 --> 00:08:20.370
I'm serious. You're lucky
to be alive after that blast.

79
00:08:20.614 --> 00:08:21.410
What blast?

80
00:08:21.614 --> 00:08:23.093
The underground gas main.

81
00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:25.450
You should exercise caution
before firing...

82
00:08:25.694 --> 00:08:28.003
...l'll tell you that now.
Especially you.

83
00:08:29.494 --> 00:08:32.292
Have yourself checked out with EMS
before you leave.

84
00:08:44.614 --> 00:08:46.127
I'm sorry about back there.

85
00:08:46.374 --> 00:08:47.568
It happens.

86
00:08:47.814 --> 00:08:49.247
Didn't used to.

87
00:08:51.214 --> 00:08:53.444
The spirit's willing, Kay...

88
00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.452
...but the rest of me...

89
00:08:59.254 --> 00:09:01.131
They're beautiful, aren't they?

90
00:09:01.894 --> 00:09:03.373
The stars.

91
00:09:04.454 --> 00:09:06.410
We never just look anymore.

92
00:09:11.814 --> 00:09:13.406
I'll tell you, Kay...

93
00:09:14.254 --> 00:09:16.324
...I will miss the chase.

94
00:09:21.414 --> 00:09:22.244
No, Dee...

95
00:09:23.374 --> 00:09:24.489
...you won't.

96
00:09:26.254 --> 00:09:27.653
Freeze!

97
00:09:27.854 --> 00:09:29.924
NYPD! Freeze!

98
00:09:31.334 --> 00:09:32.608
All yours, Edwards.

99
00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.047
Freeze means stop!

100
00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:43.847
What the hell?!

101
00:09:52.014 --> 00:09:54.733
It just be raining black people
in New York.

102
00:10:18.894 --> 00:10:20.373
Do you see this?

103
00:10:20.614 --> 00:10:22.491
N-Y-P-D!

104
00:10:22.694 --> 00:10:25.162
Means I will knock your punk-ass down!

105
00:10:25.414 --> 00:10:26.688
He's coming!

106
00:10:26.934 --> 00:10:29.607
Yeah, and when he gets here,
I'll arrest his ass too.

107
00:10:33.334 --> 00:10:35.529
You trying to catch a beat-down?

108
00:11:40.174 --> 00:11:41.289
What's up?

109
00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:44.162
He's coming.

110
00:11:44.454 --> 00:11:47.127
He's coming because I failed.
Now he'll kill me.

111
00:11:47.374 --> 00:11:49.569
You pissing everybody off today, huh?

112
00:11:51.334 --> 00:11:52.926
You don't understand.

113
00:11:53.174 --> 00:11:55.244
Your world's gonna end.

114
00:11:58.214 --> 00:11:59.329
What are you?

115
00:12:05.094 --> 00:12:07.289
Watch that ledge. Watch the ledge.

116
00:12:07.534 --> 00:12:10.685
Come on down. We'll get those
eyes fixed, don't worry.

117
00:12:10.934 --> 00:12:13.004
Wait a minute.
Let me talk to you!

118
00:12:20.334 --> 00:12:22.290
I work my butt off to make a living.

119
00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:25.685
All I want is to come home to
a fat steak on the table...

120
00:12:25.934 --> 00:12:28.084
...but instead I get this.
It looks like poison.

121
00:12:28.454 --> 00:12:32.413
Don't take that away! I'm eating that!
It is poison, isn't it?

122
00:12:32.654 --> 00:12:35.122
I swear, I wouldn't
be surprised if it was...

123
00:12:35.374 --> 00:12:38.810
...the way you skulk like a dog
been hit too much, or not enough!

124
00:12:39.054 --> 00:12:40.248
I can't decide.

125
00:12:40.494 --> 00:12:42.052
You're useless, Beatrice.

126
00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:46.253
The only thing that pulls its weight
around here is my goddamn truck!

127
00:12:56.054 --> 00:12:57.407
Figures.

128
00:13:06.094 --> 00:13:07.573
What the heck is it?

129
00:13:08.814 --> 00:13:10.850
Get your big butt back in the house.

130
00:13:22.934 --> 00:13:26.165
Place projectile weapon on the ground.

131
00:13:26.414 --> 00:13:28.052
You can have my gun...

132
00:13:28.254 --> 00:13:30.324
...when you pry it
from my dead fingers.

133
00:13:30.574 --> 00:13:32.804
Your proposal is acceptable.

134
00:14:13.414 --> 00:14:15.086
Edgar, what on earth was that?

135
00:14:15.334 --> 00:14:16.449
Sugar.

136
00:14:16.814 --> 00:14:19.044
I've never seen sugar do that.

137
00:14:20.174 --> 00:14:22.244
Give me sugar.

138
00:14:26.774 --> 00:14:28.002
In water.

139
00:14:34.214 --> 00:14:35.329
More.

140
00:14:38.774 --> 00:14:39.843
More.

141
00:14:53.814 --> 00:14:55.805
Your skin is hanging off your bones.

142
00:15:07.094 --> 00:15:08.083
Is that better?

143
00:15:36.334 --> 00:15:38.848
"The perpetrator blinked
two sets of eyelids."

144
00:15:39.094 --> 00:15:40.732
Blinked with both eyes?

145
00:15:40.934 --> 00:15:43.892
He blinked one set,
then a completely different set.

146
00:15:44.134 --> 00:15:46.523
You know, like high beams
and low beams.

147
00:15:47.654 --> 00:15:51.283
Was that before or after he drew
the weapon that you claim...

148
00:15:51.534 --> 00:15:53.570
...evaporated into a million pieces?

149
00:15:53.814 --> 00:15:55.372
After, sir.

150
00:15:56.214 --> 00:15:59.763
Why is it that no other officers saw
either of these events?

151
00:16:00.014 --> 00:16:02.482
Some of them are
soggy around the midsection.

152
00:16:02.734 --> 00:16:04.247
They weren't able to keep up.

153
00:16:04.454 --> 00:16:06.410
If you were half the man I am...

154
00:16:06.734 --> 00:16:09.089
I am half the man that you are.

155
00:16:09.334 --> 00:16:10.892
What is your problem?

156
00:16:11.134 --> 00:16:12.203
You're in my face.

157
00:16:12.454 --> 00:16:14.843
- I think he threw him off the roof.
- You next.

158
00:16:15.054 --> 00:16:16.043
I wanna talk to you.

159
00:16:16.254 --> 00:16:18.848
Ten minutes,
you take your best shot, tough guy.

160
00:16:19.734 --> 00:16:23.249
Take 10 minutes on a StairMaster,
you pudgy bastard!

161
00:16:28.294 --> 00:16:30.683
I believe you. Laurel Weaver.
Deputy Medical Examiner.

162
00:16:30.934 --> 00:16:32.925
Find me at the morgue. I'll show you.

163
00:16:33.134 --> 00:16:33.930
Wait.

164
00:16:34.254 --> 00:16:35.164
Wait a minute!

165
00:16:36.174 --> 00:16:40.213
You're Dr. Weaver with the coroner's
office working on the John Doe?

166
00:16:40.414 --> 00:16:42.848
- That's right.
- Will you look at this, please?

167
00:16:49.774 --> 00:16:51.173
Some night, huh?

168
00:16:51.494 --> 00:16:52.290
Some night.

169
00:16:52.494 --> 00:16:54.371
They were gills, not eyelids.

170
00:16:55.734 --> 00:16:57.611
Gills. He was out of breath.

171
00:16:58.414 --> 00:16:59.483
Who are you?

172
00:16:59.734 --> 00:17:01.326
Did he say anything to you?

173
00:17:01.574 --> 00:17:03.451
He said the world was
coming to an end.

174
00:17:04.494 --> 00:17:05.813
Did he say when?

175
00:17:11.654 --> 00:17:14.293
Would you recognize his weapon
if you saw it again?

176
00:17:14.534 --> 00:17:15.853
Absolutely.

177
00:17:17.414 --> 00:17:19.006
Come on, let's take a ride.

178
00:17:19.254 --> 00:17:21.893
Wait a minute. Look, I got
tons of paperwork...

179
00:17:22.134 --> 00:17:22.964
It's all done.

180
00:17:23.214 --> 00:17:24.044
Good work.

181
00:17:24.294 --> 00:17:27.092
You really ran this dude down on foot?
That's tough.

182
00:17:27.334 --> 00:17:28.813
That's double tough.

183
00:17:38.334 --> 00:17:38.734
So who exactly are you with?

184
00:17:38.734 --> 00:17:40.452
So who exactly are you with?

185
00:17:40.694 --> 00:17:42.764
FBI? NSA?

186
00:17:43.014 --> 00:17:47.371
I'm part of a bureau that licenses,
monitors and polices aliens on Earth.

187
00:17:47.614 --> 00:17:48.842
Yeah, whatever.

188
00:17:49.054 --> 00:17:50.248
We're here.

189
00:17:52.134 --> 00:17:53.772
This is where we're going?

190
00:17:54.494 --> 00:17:55.847
This is Jack Jeebs' spot.

191
00:17:56.054 --> 00:17:58.284
He buys from chain-snatchers.
Doesn't sell guns.

192
00:17:58.534 --> 00:17:59.523
Really?

193
00:18:00.134 --> 00:18:01.044
All right, look.

194
00:18:01.254 --> 00:18:05.213
I'm gonna go in and put my thing down,
but when I come out, I want answers.

195
00:18:05.454 --> 00:18:07.046
Okay, go put your thing down.

196
00:18:12.854 --> 00:18:14.253
Officer Eduardo!

197
00:18:14.494 --> 00:18:17.213
How did these get here?
I thought I turned them in.

198
00:18:17.454 --> 00:18:20.651
I hear you're into something hotter
than stolen Rolexes.

199
00:18:20.854 --> 00:18:23.493
I deal crack, but I still work here.
I love the hours.

200
00:18:23.934 --> 00:18:26.732
I'm talking about guns, smart-ass!
Weird ones.

201
00:18:27.334 --> 00:18:30.007
Come on!
What you see is what I got.

202
00:18:32.294 --> 00:18:33.773
Show him the imports, Jeebs.

203
00:18:34.854 --> 00:18:36.412
Hey, Kay. How are you?

204
00:18:36.654 --> 00:18:39.566
- Show him the imports.
- I got out of that business.

205
00:18:39.814 --> 00:18:41.247
Why do you lie to me?

206
00:18:41.734 --> 00:18:42.883
Hold on a second.

207
00:18:43.214 --> 00:18:44.249
I'll count to three.

208
00:18:44.494 --> 00:18:47.292
He'll do it, Jeebs.
That man does not look stable.

209
00:18:47.494 --> 00:18:50.054
You know what? He's crazy
when he's like this.

210
00:18:50.294 --> 00:18:52.171
He's always crazy.
Get a massage.

211
00:18:52.414 --> 00:18:53.244
Take a cruise...

212
00:18:54.014 --> 00:18:56.209
- Drop the weapon.
- I warned him.

213
00:18:56.454 --> 00:18:57.250
Drop the weapon!

214
00:18:57.454 --> 00:18:58.682
- You warned him.
- I'll kill you.

215
00:18:58.934 --> 00:19:01.926
You insensitive jerk!

216
00:19:05.574 --> 00:19:07.849
Do you have any idea
how much that stings?

217
00:19:08.214 --> 00:19:10.489
Show us the merchandise,
or you'll lose another head.

218
00:19:22.814 --> 00:19:23.610
Mr. Edwards...

219
00:19:28.854 --> 00:19:30.731
There, the one in the middle.

220
00:19:33.774 --> 00:19:37.210
You sold a reverberating carbonizer
with mutate capacity...

221
00:19:37.454 --> 00:19:39.763
...to an unlicensed cephalopoid!
You piece of...

222
00:19:40.214 --> 00:19:41.442
He looked okay to me.

223
00:19:41.654 --> 00:19:43.485
It was for an assassination.
The target?

224
00:19:43.734 --> 00:19:44.610
I don't know.

225
00:19:44.814 --> 00:19:46.611
- Goddamn it!
- I don't know!

226
00:19:48.014 --> 00:19:49.288
All that's confiscated.

227
00:19:49.534 --> 00:19:53.447
Be on the next transport off this rock,
or I shoot where it don't grow back.

228
00:19:57.374 --> 00:20:00.286
And I'm gonna be back
to talk about them Rolexes.

229
00:20:22.014 --> 00:20:24.084
Searching for a handle on the moment?

230
00:20:25.734 --> 00:20:27.167
I can't help you.

231
00:20:28.094 --> 00:20:29.607
The only comfort I can offer...

232
00:20:29.854 --> 00:20:33.051
...is my promise that tomorrow
you won't remember a thing.

233
00:20:33.574 --> 00:20:36.088
That's not exactly
some shit you forget.

234
00:20:36.334 --> 00:20:37.733
Ever seen one of these?

235
00:20:41.134 --> 00:20:43.443
She looks over to her husband...

236
00:20:43.694 --> 00:20:46.652
...then sets it down in her lap
and says:

237
00:20:46.854 --> 00:20:49.926
" Honey, this one's eating my popcorn."

238
00:20:53.094 --> 00:20:54.083
Get it?

239
00:20:54.334 --> 00:20:55.608
This one's eating...

240
00:20:57.894 --> 00:20:59.930
Gotta go.
Thanks for the egg rolls.

241
00:21:00.174 --> 00:21:01.402
Wait a minute.

242
00:21:01.694 --> 00:21:02.490
Who are you?

243
00:21:02.734 --> 00:21:05.202
See what I mean about tequila?
You're very bright.

244
00:21:05.454 --> 00:21:07.126
But you need to lay off the sauce.

245
00:21:07.374 --> 00:21:09.524
I'll see you bright and early, 9:00.

246
00:21:09.774 --> 00:21:10.570
Be there...

247
00:21:11.334 --> 00:21:12.813
...or be square.

248
00:21:33.174 --> 00:21:34.653
Well, well, well.

249
00:21:34.894 --> 00:21:38.045
Moving right in, are we?
Think we own the place?

250
00:21:38.254 --> 00:21:40.085
I got an eviction notice for you.

251
00:21:40.334 --> 00:21:43.007
Just what exactly
do you think you're doing here?

252
00:21:43.254 --> 00:21:45.210
Taking care of your pest problem.

253
00:21:45.454 --> 00:21:46.728
Pest problem?

254
00:21:47.574 --> 00:21:48.723
Pest?

255
00:21:48.934 --> 00:21:50.845
You got a hell of an infestation.

256
00:21:51.054 --> 00:21:53.773
You know, I've noticed
an infestation here.

257
00:21:53.974 --> 00:21:56.647
Everywhere I look, nothing but
undeveloped, unevolved...

258
00:21:56.894 --> 00:21:59.283
...barely conscious pond scum...

259
00:21:59.494 --> 00:22:02.054
...totally convinced
of their own superiority...

260
00:22:02.294 --> 00:22:04.285
...as they scurry about their short...

261
00:22:04.534 --> 00:22:06.206
...pointless lives.

262
00:22:09.094 --> 00:22:10.846
Don't you wanna get rid of them?

263
00:22:11.094 --> 00:22:12.732
In the worst way.

264
00:22:47.094 --> 00:22:48.447
Help you?

265
00:22:48.814 --> 00:22:50.645
This dude gave me this card...

266
00:22:50.894 --> 00:22:52.122
Elevator.

267
00:23:15.854 --> 00:23:18.004
You're late. Sit down.

268
00:23:24.734 --> 00:23:26.133
My name is Zed.

269
00:23:26.534 --> 00:23:29.048
You're all here
because you're the best.

270
00:23:29.254 --> 00:23:33.645
Marines, Air Force, Navy SEALs,
Army Rangers, NYPD.

271
00:23:34.014 --> 00:23:35.129
We want one of you.

272
00:23:35.654 --> 00:23:36.723
Just one.

273
00:23:36.974 --> 00:23:39.613
What will follow is
a series of simple tests...

274
00:23:39.854 --> 00:23:43.244
...for motor skills,
concentration, stamina.

275
00:23:43.974 --> 00:23:45.327
I see we have a question.

276
00:23:45.574 --> 00:23:49.010
I'm sorry, maybe you
already answered this but...

277
00:23:49.254 --> 00:23:50.607
...why are we here?

278
00:23:50.854 --> 00:23:51.809
Son.

279
00:23:52.294 --> 00:23:55.092
Lieutenant Jensen.
West Point graduate with honours.

280
00:23:55.334 --> 00:23:58.804
We're here because you want
the best of the best of the best, sir!

281
00:24:04.174 --> 00:24:05.926
What's so funny, Edwards?

282
00:24:06.294 --> 00:24:08.285
Your boy, Captain America, here.

283
00:24:08.894 --> 00:24:11.328
"The best of the best
of the best, sir!"

284
00:24:11.654 --> 00:24:12.450
"With honours."

285
00:24:13.254 --> 00:24:14.812
He's just really excited...

286
00:24:15.014 --> 00:24:17.005
...and has no clue why we're here.

287
00:24:17.254 --> 00:24:19.563
That's just very funny to me.

288
00:24:20.934 --> 00:24:22.526
Y'all ain't laughing, though.

289
00:24:30.054 --> 00:24:31.885
Okay, let's get going.

290
00:25:53.054 --> 00:25:54.248
Wanna get down on this?

291
00:26:19.134 --> 00:26:20.726
Edwards, what happened?

292
00:26:21.734 --> 00:26:22.530
Hesitated.

293
00:26:25.254 --> 00:26:28.803
May I ask why you felt
little Tiffany deserved to die?

294
00:26:29.054 --> 00:26:31.329
She was the only one
that seemed dangerous.

295
00:26:31.534 --> 00:26:32.887
How'd you figure that?

296
00:26:33.094 --> 00:26:35.688
I was gonna pop this guy
hanging from the light...

297
00:26:35.934 --> 00:26:37.447
...but he's just working out.

298
00:26:37.734 --> 00:26:41.249
How'd I feel if somebody bust
my ass while I'm on the treadmill?

299
00:26:41.494 --> 00:26:43.291
Then I saw this snarling beast.

300
00:26:43.534 --> 00:26:46.446
I noticed he had a tissue
in his hand and realized...

301
00:26:46.694 --> 00:26:48.650
...he's not snarling,
he's sneezing.

302
00:26:48.894 --> 00:26:50.168
Ain't no threat there.

303
00:26:50.414 --> 00:26:51.449
Then I saw Tiffany.

304
00:26:51.694 --> 00:26:54.492
8-year-old white girl,
middle of the ghetto...

305
00:26:54.734 --> 00:26:57.453
...bunch of monsters at night
with quantum physics books?

306
00:26:57.734 --> 00:26:59.452
She about to start some shit.

307
00:26:59.654 --> 00:27:02.088
Those books are
way too advanced for her.

308
00:27:02.334 --> 00:27:04.609
If you ask me, she's up to something.

309
00:27:04.894 --> 00:27:07.488
I'd appreciate it if you
eased up about it.

310
00:27:11.494 --> 00:27:13.405
Or do I owe her an apology?

311
00:27:20.734 --> 00:27:22.087
Good shot, though, right?

312
00:27:27.414 --> 00:27:29.245
He has a problem with authority.

313
00:27:29.494 --> 00:27:30.722
So do I.

314
00:27:31.014 --> 00:27:34.051
But this kid ran down
a cephalopoid on foot, boss.

315
00:27:34.294 --> 00:27:36.046
That's gotta be tough enough.

316
00:27:37.134 --> 00:27:39.250
Let's hope you know what you're doing.

317
00:27:47.334 --> 00:27:49.404
Gentlemen, congratulations.

318
00:27:49.614 --> 00:27:53.004
You're everything we expect
from years of government training.

319
00:27:53.214 --> 00:27:56.684
If you'll just follow me,
we have one more test to administer.

320
00:27:56.894 --> 00:27:58.486
An eye exam.

321
00:28:10.894 --> 00:28:12.122
Where are you going?

322
00:28:13.894 --> 00:28:15.327
What the hell is all this?

323
00:28:15.574 --> 00:28:18.566
In the 1950s, the government
started an underfunded agency...

324
00:28:18.814 --> 00:28:21.453
...with the laughable purpose
of establishing contact...

325
00:28:21.654 --> 00:28:23.372
...with a race not of this planet.

326
00:28:23.574 --> 00:28:25.644
Look at the end of this device.

327
00:28:25.974 --> 00:28:28.772
Everyone thought the agency
was a joke, except the aliens...

328
00:28:29.014 --> 00:28:31.972
...who made contact on March 2, 1961
outside New York.

329
00:28:32.214 --> 00:28:36.093
There were nine of us the first night.
Seven agents, one astronomer...

330
00:28:36.294 --> 00:28:38.364
...and a dumb kid who'd gotten lost.

331
00:28:38.614 --> 00:28:41.333
You brought that tall man some flowers.

332
00:28:41.934 --> 00:28:43.049
This way.

333
00:28:44.134 --> 00:28:46.364
They were a group
of intergalactic refugees.

334
00:28:46.614 --> 00:28:50.084
Wanted Earth as an apolitical zone
for creatures without a planet.

335
00:28:50.334 --> 00:28:51.813
You ever see <i>Casablanca</i>?

336
00:28:52.054 --> 00:28:53.646
Same thing, except no Nazis.

337
00:28:53.854 --> 00:28:57.051
We agreed and concealed
all evidence of their landing.

338
00:28:57.974 --> 00:29:01.933
So these are real flying saucers
and the World's Fair was a cover-up?

339
00:29:02.214 --> 00:29:03.283
Why hold it in Queens?

340
00:29:03.534 --> 00:29:06.332
More nonhumans arrive every year
and live among us in secret.

341
00:29:06.574 --> 00:29:11.125
Not to change the subject, but when
was the last time you got a CAT scan?

342
00:29:11.374 --> 00:29:14.889
- Six months ago. It's company policy.
- Make another appointment.

343
00:29:15.134 --> 00:29:18.206
Tell your boy Zed I had
an absolutely wonderful time...

344
00:29:18.454 --> 00:29:21.366
...and thank you for everything,
but show me the door.

345
00:29:21.614 --> 00:29:24.572
All right. I'm getting some coffee.
You want some?

346
00:29:24.814 --> 00:29:26.532
No, thank you, I'm fine.

347
00:29:31.694 --> 00:29:32.683
How you doing?

348
00:29:32.934 --> 00:29:34.049
Hi, Kay.

349
00:29:35.214 --> 00:29:37.603
- That's not decaf, is it?
- Viennese cinnamon.

350
00:29:38.014 --> 00:29:41.768
Don't tell me we only got powdered
stuff for cream. I hate it.

351
00:29:43.654 --> 00:29:45.770
Well, that's good. Good. Good.

352
00:29:46.614 --> 00:29:48.252
You guys getting along all right?

353
00:29:49.814 --> 00:29:51.247
Don't work too hard.

354
00:29:54.934 --> 00:29:56.845
Sure you don't want some coffee?

355
00:30:03.054 --> 00:30:04.487
Here's the deal.

356
00:30:04.734 --> 00:30:07.931
At any given time, there are
around 1500 aliens on the planet.

357
00:30:08.174 --> 00:30:10.051
Most of them here in Manhattan.

358
00:30:10.294 --> 00:30:13.047
Most of them are decent.
Just trying to make a living.

359
00:30:13.294 --> 00:30:15.649
- Cab drivers?
- Not as many as you'd think.

360
00:30:16.134 --> 00:30:19.126
Humans, for the most part,
don't have a clue. Don't want one.

361
00:30:19.374 --> 00:30:23.652
They're happy. They think
they have a good bead on things.

362
00:30:24.494 --> 00:30:26.883
People are smart.
They can handle it.

363
00:30:27.214 --> 00:30:28.203
A person is smart.

364
00:30:28.534 --> 00:30:32.129
People are dumb, panicky,
dangerous animals, and you know it.

365
00:30:32.494 --> 00:30:35.486
1500 years ago, everybody knew
the Earth was...

366
00:30:35.734 --> 00:30:37.372
...the centre of the universe.

367
00:30:37.614 --> 00:30:40.811
500 years ago, everybody knew
the Earth was flat.

368
00:30:41.054 --> 00:30:44.933
And 15 minutes ago, you knew that
people were alone on this planet.

369
00:30:46.934 --> 00:30:48.890
Imagine what you'll know...

370
00:30:49.094 --> 00:30:50.209
...tomorrow.

371
00:30:52.534 --> 00:30:54.650
- What's the catch?
- The catch?

372
00:30:55.214 --> 00:30:57.603
The catch is, you will sever
all human contact.

373
00:30:57.854 --> 00:31:00.812
Nobody will ever know
you exist anywhere...

374
00:31:02.654 --> 00:31:03.643
...ever.

375
00:31:06.854 --> 00:31:09.243
I'll give you to sunrise
to think it over.

376
00:31:14.174 --> 00:31:15.448
Is it worth it?

377
00:31:15.694 --> 00:31:17.013
Yeah, it's worth it.

378
00:31:19.414 --> 00:31:20.972
If you're strong enough.

379
00:32:18.734 --> 00:32:20.053
What's up, pops?

380
00:32:30.214 --> 00:32:31.124
I'm in...

381
00:32:31.334 --> 00:32:34.531
...because there's some
next-level shit going on here.

382
00:32:34.734 --> 00:32:37.851
Before y'all beam me up,
there's a few things to understand.

383
00:32:38.094 --> 00:32:41.689
First off, you chose me,
so you recognize the skills.

384
00:32:41.934 --> 00:32:45.404
I don't want nobody calling me
"son" or " kid" or "sport." Cool?

385
00:32:45.654 --> 00:32:46.848
Cool. Whatever, slick.

386
00:32:47.054 --> 00:32:50.171
But I need to tell you something
about all your skills.

387
00:32:51.414 --> 00:32:52.294
As of right now,
they mean precisely...

388
00:32:52.294 --> 00:32:54.524
As of right now,
they mean precisely...

389
00:32:54.934 --> 00:32:56.162
...dick.

390
00:33:08.854 --> 00:33:11.243
- Purpose of trip?
- Diplomatic mission.

391
00:33:11.494 --> 00:33:12.370
Duration of stay?

392
00:33:12.614 --> 00:33:13.842
Lunch.

393
00:33:14.094 --> 00:33:15.846
Any fruits or vegetables?

394
00:33:27.854 --> 00:33:30.209
You wanna stay away from that guy.

395
00:33:31.374 --> 00:33:32.727
He's grouchy.

396
00:33:33.134 --> 00:33:35.967
Three hours in customs
after a 17-trillion-mile trip...

397
00:33:36.174 --> 00:33:37.607
...will make anyone cranky.

398
00:33:37.814 --> 00:33:39.645
What government branch
do we report to?

399
00:33:39.894 --> 00:33:42.362
- None. They ask too many questions.
- Who pays for this?

400
00:33:42.574 --> 00:33:46.852
We hold patents on a few gadgets we
confiscated from out-of-state visitors.

401
00:33:47.094 --> 00:33:49.164
Velcro, microwave ovens, liposuction.

402
00:33:49.374 --> 00:33:51.171
This is a fascinating gadget.

403
00:33:51.694 --> 00:33:55.084
It'll replace CDs soon. I'll have to
buy the White Album again.

404
00:33:55.334 --> 00:33:59.293
That's fun. A universal translator.
We're not even supposed to have it.

405
00:33:59.534 --> 00:34:02.002
Human thought is so primitive.
It's looked upon...

406
00:34:02.254 --> 00:34:04.688
...as an infectious disease
in some galaxies.

407
00:34:04.934 --> 00:34:06.686
That kind of makes you proud.

408
00:34:06.934 --> 00:34:07.969
What's this?

409
00:34:11.654 --> 00:34:12.848
Just be calm!

410
00:34:13.094 --> 00:34:14.083
Relax!

411
00:34:14.774 --> 00:34:16.048
Watch your head!

412
00:34:16.534 --> 00:34:18.172
Someone get him some ice!

413
00:34:18.974 --> 00:34:21.966
Look out! Move! Just move
when it's coming at you!

414
00:34:27.934 --> 00:34:28.730
Damn!

415
00:34:29.454 --> 00:34:30.967
I'll pay for that!

416
00:34:41.814 --> 00:34:44.806
This thing caused
the 1977 New York blackout.

417
00:34:45.734 --> 00:34:47.770
Practical joke
by the Great Attractor.

418
00:34:48.014 --> 00:34:49.572
He thought it was funny.

419
00:34:50.894 --> 00:34:52.122
Sorry, y'all.

420
00:34:52.774 --> 00:34:54.810
It was a accident. Sorry.

421
00:34:55.334 --> 00:34:57.325
Observation,
the heart of our endeavour.

422
00:34:57.574 --> 00:34:59.644
Meet the twins, Blblup and Bob.

423
00:34:59.894 --> 00:35:03.091
This map shows the location
of every alien on Earth.

424
00:35:03.334 --> 00:35:05.245
Some are under constant surveillance.

425
00:35:05.614 --> 00:35:07.605
Everyone on those screens is an alien.

426
00:35:07.854 --> 00:35:10.607
In public, they're as normal
as you are, but in private...

427
00:35:11.174 --> 00:35:12.129
You'll get the idea.

428
00:35:13.294 --> 00:35:14.613
Oh, man.

429
00:35:15.054 --> 00:35:16.612
Doesn't make any sense, right?

430
00:35:17.774 --> 00:35:20.334
Well, no, it makes perfect sense.

431
00:35:20.854 --> 00:35:24.005
In third grade, everyone said
I was crazy, but I knew our teacher...

432
00:35:24.214 --> 00:35:26.364
...had to be from Venus or something.

433
00:35:26.574 --> 00:35:29.213
Ms. Edelson. Jupiter, actually.
Well, one of the moons.

434
00:35:30.574 --> 00:35:31.404
...revolve.

435
00:35:31.654 --> 00:35:32.928
Class...

436
00:35:33.374 --> 00:35:35.649
...be quiet and pay attention!

437
00:35:36.574 --> 00:35:38.132
If I have to tell you...

438
00:35:38.334 --> 00:35:40.609
...one more time...

439
00:35:42.254 --> 00:35:43.403
Let's put it on.

440
00:35:44.214 --> 00:35:45.010
Put what on?

441
00:35:45.614 --> 00:35:48.003
The last suit you'll ever wear.

442
00:36:00.014 --> 00:36:02.608
<i>You will dress only in attire</i>
<i>specially sanctioned... </i>

443
00:36:02.854 --> 00:36:04.765
<i>... by MiB Special Services. </i>

444
00:36:05.254 --> 00:36:07.927
<i>You'll conform to</i>
<i>the identity we give you... </i>

445
00:36:08.174 --> 00:36:10.847
<i>... eat where we tell you, </i>
<i>live where we tell you. </i>

446
00:36:11.454 --> 00:36:12.364
<i>From now on... </i>

447
00:36:12.614 --> 00:36:15.003
<i>... you'll have no identifying</i>
<i>marks of any kind. </i>

448
00:36:15.254 --> 00:36:17.768
<i>You will not stand out in any way. </i>

449
00:36:18.174 --> 00:36:19.971
<i>Your entire image is crafted... </i>

450
00:36:20.214 --> 00:36:23.012
<i>... to leave no lasting memory</i>
<i>with anyone you meet. </i>

451
00:36:23.334 --> 00:36:25.643
<i>You are a rumour, </i>
<i>recognizable only as... </i>

452
00:36:25.854 --> 00:36:28.607
<i>... déjà vu and dismissed</i>
<i>just as quickly. </i>

453
00:36:28.854 --> 00:36:31.084
<i>You don't exist. </i>
<i>You were never born. </i>

454
00:36:33.734 --> 00:36:35.611
<i>Anonymity is your name. </i>

455
00:36:35.854 --> 00:36:37.651
<i>Silence, your native tongue. </i>

456
00:36:38.414 --> 00:36:40.609
<i>You're no longer part of the system. </i>

457
00:36:40.814 --> 00:36:42.884
<i>You are above the system. Over it. </i>

458
00:36:43.374 --> 00:36:44.853
<i>Beyond it. </i>

459
00:36:45.974 --> 00:36:48.044
<i>We're "them. " We're "they. "</i>

460
00:36:48.414 --> 00:36:50.769
<i>We are the Men in Black. </i>

461
00:36:57.814 --> 00:37:00.772
You know what the difference is
between you and me?

462
00:37:03.214 --> 00:37:05.091
I make this look good.

463
00:37:07.174 --> 00:37:09.051
We're gonna go for a little ride.

464
00:37:09.454 --> 00:37:12.969
I'll put you down here for a minute,
and Daddy will be right back.

465
00:37:43.134 --> 00:37:45.887
Okay, now we're ready to go
for a little ride.

466
00:37:46.134 --> 00:37:49.570
We'll meet one of Daddy's friends,
and you'll like him.

467
00:37:52.494 --> 00:37:54.371
Okay, let's see.

468
00:37:55.014 --> 00:37:58.324
Bee, we got the deposed sur-prefect
of Singalee...

469
00:37:58.574 --> 00:38:01.372
...touching down in the forest
outside Portland tonight.

470
00:38:01.614 --> 00:38:04.128
<i>-Humanoid? </i>
- You wish. Bring a sponge.

471
00:38:05.294 --> 00:38:07.285
Here. Red letter from last night.

472
00:38:07.974 --> 00:38:10.807
We had an unauthorized landing
in upstate New York.

473
00:38:11.054 --> 00:38:12.965
Keep your ears open
on this one.

474
00:38:13.174 --> 00:38:16.450
We're not hosting an
intergalactic kegger down here.

475
00:38:18.254 --> 00:38:19.653
We got a skimmer.

476
00:38:20.014 --> 00:38:21.845
Landed alien out of zone.
Who is it?

477
00:38:22.094 --> 00:38:23.083
Redgick.

478
00:38:23.334 --> 00:38:26.212
He's not cleared to leave Manhattan,
but he's out of town...

479
00:38:26.454 --> 00:38:28.410
...stuck on the New Jersey turnpike.

480
00:38:28.654 --> 00:38:30.292
Take junior with you.

481
00:38:30.534 --> 00:38:33.207
This is a good one
for him to warm up on.

482
00:38:33.774 --> 00:38:34.729
Go get him, tiger.

483
00:38:41.414 --> 00:38:43.974
"We're not hosting
an intergalactic kegger."

484
00:38:45.254 --> 00:38:46.403
Zed...

485
00:38:47.334 --> 00:38:48.449
He just...

486
00:38:49.974 --> 00:38:53.762
Unlimited technology from the
whole universe, and we cruise around...

487
00:38:53.974 --> 00:38:55.373
...in a Ford POS.

488
00:38:57.814 --> 00:38:59.566
Fasten your seat belt.

489
00:38:59.814 --> 00:39:01.566
We gotta work on your people skills.

490
00:39:01.814 --> 00:39:04.408
You'd get a better reaction
if you were polite.

491
00:39:04.654 --> 00:39:06.212
Fasten your seat belt, please.

492
00:39:06.414 --> 00:39:07.972
Good. Did you hurt yourself?

493
00:39:11.654 --> 00:39:15.169
The red button there, kid.
Don't ever touch the red button.

494
00:39:24.774 --> 00:39:27.334
All right, pop,
that'll be $72 there.

495
00:39:27.934 --> 00:39:31.006
Okay, sweetie, let me pay
the impolite driver.

496
00:39:59.574 --> 00:40:03.647
Sorry I'm late. The cab drivers
on this planet are terrible.

497
00:40:03.894 --> 00:40:06.169
Your Majesty,
you are in grave danger.

498
00:40:06.414 --> 00:40:09.292
Yeah, and they overcharge
you every time.

499
00:40:09.534 --> 00:40:13.209
Sir, a bug landed here.
We must get you off the planet.

500
00:40:13.454 --> 00:40:15.570
A bug? He must know
why I'm here.

501
00:40:15.814 --> 00:40:17.247
We think he does.

502
00:40:18.734 --> 00:40:20.406
Is that what I think it is?

503
00:40:20.654 --> 00:40:23.043
No, just some diamonds
for your children.

504
00:40:23.294 --> 00:40:24.443
Do we have time to eat?

505
00:40:25.214 --> 00:40:28.445
Sure. I ordered you
some Pirogi.

506
00:40:31.534 --> 00:40:32.967
Six is up!

507
00:40:34.254 --> 00:40:35.243
Where is lvan?

508
00:40:35.494 --> 00:40:36.927
Gave him a break.

509
00:40:47.174 --> 00:40:50.086
To the continued reign of
the Arquillian Empire.

510
00:40:50.334 --> 00:40:52.211
To the safety of the Galaxy.

511
00:40:59.214 --> 00:41:02.126
You can kill us both,
but you will not find the Galaxy.

512
00:41:03.054 --> 00:41:05.124
You're right about one thing.

513
00:41:18.934 --> 00:41:20.492
You're not going anywhere.

514
00:41:36.814 --> 00:41:38.884
Your licence and registration, please.

515
00:41:42.454 --> 00:41:45.446
Like to see your other licence
and registration, please.

516
00:41:52.174 --> 00:41:55.849
You're restricted to Manhattan.
Where are you going, Redgie?

517
00:41:56.614 --> 00:41:59.048
It's my wife. She's...
Well, look.

518
00:42:03.654 --> 00:42:04.769
No big deal.

519
00:42:05.014 --> 00:42:07.050
Okay, you come with me, Redge.

520
00:42:09.134 --> 00:42:11.125
And you handle this.

521
00:42:11.374 --> 00:42:12.204
What?! Me?

522
00:42:12.934 --> 00:42:15.209
- You just catch.
- Does he know what he's doing?

523
00:42:15.414 --> 00:42:17.405
He does it all the time.
Let him work.

524
00:42:25.774 --> 00:42:27.446
Damn, man!

525
00:42:28.254 --> 00:42:30.814
Something's peeking!

526
00:42:31.054 --> 00:42:32.931
You're headed out of town.

527
00:42:33.174 --> 00:42:35.369
- We're meeting someone.
- Who?

528
00:42:35.614 --> 00:42:38.492
- It's a ship.
- I saw no departure clearance.

529
00:42:38.734 --> 00:42:39.564
You didn't?

530
00:42:39.814 --> 00:42:41.964
It's an emergency.

531
00:42:42.534 --> 00:42:43.808
You're doing fine!

532
00:42:44.014 --> 00:42:47.973
What kind of emergency?
What's the rush to get off the planet?

533
00:42:48.294 --> 00:42:50.364
We don't like
the neighbourhood anymore.

534
00:42:50.614 --> 00:42:52.366
Some of the new arrivals...

535
00:42:52.614 --> 00:42:55.811
New arrivals? Have anything to do
with the crasher last night?

536
00:42:56.014 --> 00:42:57.333
Excuse me, miss!

537
00:43:00.854 --> 00:43:02.253
Oh, man.

538
00:43:02.814 --> 00:43:04.452
Oh, man!

539
00:43:06.414 --> 00:43:07.290
Look.

540
00:43:07.534 --> 00:43:09.252
Oh, man!

541
00:43:10.734 --> 00:43:12.804
Congratulations, Redge.
It's a...

542
00:43:13.654 --> 00:43:14.973
...squid.

543
00:43:18.214 --> 00:43:19.090
You know, it's...

544
00:43:20.054 --> 00:43:21.885
...actually kind of...

545
00:43:27.974 --> 00:43:29.089
...cute.

546
00:43:36.654 --> 00:43:38.724
Anything about that seem unusual?

547
00:43:41.254 --> 00:43:42.767
What would scare Redgick so badly...

548
00:43:43.014 --> 00:43:45.369
...that he'd risk a warp jump
with a newborn?

549
00:43:45.814 --> 00:43:47.645
We'll check the hot sheets.

550
00:43:53.054 --> 00:43:54.203
These are " hot sheets"?

551
00:43:54.414 --> 00:43:56.370
Best investigative reporting on Earth.

552
00:43:56.614 --> 00:43:59.572
Read <i>The New York Times</i> if you want.
They get lucky sometimes.

553
00:43:59.934 --> 00:44:03.483
Cannot believe you're looking for tips
in the supermarket tabloids.

554
00:44:04.934 --> 00:44:06.367
Not " looking for."

555
00:44:07.214 --> 00:44:09.774
Found.

556
00:44:21.974 --> 00:44:24.249
- Wait a minute, slow down.
- Why?

557
00:44:24.494 --> 00:44:27.566
Give her time to get the wrong
impression. Makes it smoother.

558
00:44:28.654 --> 00:44:30.007
Can I help you?

559
00:44:30.254 --> 00:44:33.405
Yes, ma'am. I'm Agent Manheim,
this is Agent Black, FBI.

560
00:44:33.654 --> 00:44:35.292
We'd like to talk about your visitor.

561
00:44:35.534 --> 00:44:36.887
Gonna make fun of me too?

562
00:44:37.134 --> 00:44:41.047
No, we do not have a sense of humour
we're aware of. May we come in?

563
00:44:42.734 --> 00:44:43.564
Sure.

564
00:44:44.014 --> 00:44:45.163
- Thank you.
- Lemonade?

565
00:44:45.414 --> 00:44:46.767
Oh, yes, please.

566
00:44:51.214 --> 00:44:53.523
The chief of police came
to the house...

567
00:44:53.774 --> 00:44:55.651
...and did an investigation.

568
00:44:56.134 --> 00:44:59.126
Took a police report and writ down
everything I said...

569
00:44:59.374 --> 00:45:01.092
...not believing one thing I said.

570
00:45:01.334 --> 00:45:02.972
Sort of poking fun at me.

571
00:45:03.214 --> 00:45:05.205
He asked me, " If he was murdered...

572
00:45:05.454 --> 00:45:07.763
...how was he able to walk
back in the house?"

573
00:45:08.014 --> 00:45:10.733
I gotta admit to you that
that one got me stumped.

574
00:45:11.134 --> 00:45:13.568
I tell you, I know Edgar,
and that wasn't Edgar.

575
00:45:15.054 --> 00:45:17.887
It was like something was
wearing Edgar.

576
00:45:19.814 --> 00:45:21.008
Like a suit...

577
00:45:21.614 --> 00:45:22.967
...an Edgar suit.

578
00:45:30.254 --> 00:45:32.848
Dude was that ugly
before he was an alien.

579
00:45:35.654 --> 00:45:37.406
I'm sorry.

580
00:45:37.774 --> 00:45:38.763
Go on.

581
00:45:39.734 --> 00:45:40.849
Anyway...

582
00:45:41.094 --> 00:45:43.050
...I come to and he's gone.

583
00:45:44.054 --> 00:45:44.964
He say anything?

584
00:45:45.294 --> 00:45:48.013
Yes. He asked me for some water.

585
00:45:48.614 --> 00:45:50.366
Some sugar water.

586
00:45:50.734 --> 00:45:51.769
Sugar water?

587
00:45:52.014 --> 00:45:54.892
I remember that right.
I thought that that was odd...

588
00:45:55.254 --> 00:45:59.167
...that he asked me for sugar water
and not lemonade or ice water...

589
00:45:59.574 --> 00:46:00.768
...or regular water...

590
00:46:01.014 --> 00:46:02.208
...tap water.

591
00:46:03.254 --> 00:46:05.814
All right, Beatrice.
There was no alien.

592
00:46:06.054 --> 00:46:08.249
The flash of light was not a U.F.O.

593
00:46:08.494 --> 00:46:12.612
Gas was trapped in a thermal pocket
and refracted the light from Venus.

594
00:46:12.854 --> 00:46:14.048
Wait a minute.

595
00:46:14.294 --> 00:46:17.570
That thing erases her memory,
and you just make up a new one?

596
00:46:17.814 --> 00:46:19.372
A standard-issue neuralizer.

597
00:46:19.614 --> 00:46:22.208
That weak-ass story is
the best you came up with?

598
00:46:22.534 --> 00:46:24.968
All right. On a more personal note...

599
00:46:25.214 --> 00:46:29.048
...Edgar ran off with an old girlfriend.
You'll stay with your mama...

600
00:46:29.294 --> 00:46:30.613
...and decide you're better off.

601
00:46:30.854 --> 00:46:34.369
Yeah, because he never
appreciated you anyway.

602
00:46:34.934 --> 00:46:36.765
In fact, you know what?

603
00:46:37.014 --> 00:46:39.608
You kicked him out.
And now that he's gone...

604
00:46:39.854 --> 00:46:42.846
...you'll go in town,
find yourself some nice dresses.

605
00:46:43.094 --> 00:46:46.973
Get yourself some shoes.
Find somewhere you could get a facial.

606
00:46:48.494 --> 00:46:51.645
And hire a decorator to come
in here quick because... damn!

607
00:46:59.454 --> 00:47:01.172
When do I get my own flashy...

608
00:47:01.414 --> 00:47:02.733
...memory messer-upper?

609
00:47:02.974 --> 00:47:03.929
When you grow up.

610
00:47:07.894 --> 00:47:08.804
Please. Not green.

611
00:47:10.254 --> 00:47:11.164
Oh, damn!

612
00:47:12.854 --> 00:47:15.573
Do you know which alien leaves
a green spectral trail...

613
00:47:15.814 --> 00:47:17.088
...and craves sugar water?

614
00:47:18.054 --> 00:47:21.729
That was on <i>Jeopardy</i> last night.
Damn, Alex said it was...

615
00:47:21.974 --> 00:47:23.726
Zed, we have a bug.

616
00:47:24.414 --> 00:47:27.053
So...
What? We don't like bugs?

617
00:47:27.294 --> 00:47:29.364
Bugs thrive on carnage, tiger.

618
00:47:29.814 --> 00:47:33.966
They consume, infest, destroy,
live off the death of other species.

619
00:47:34.214 --> 00:47:36.170
You were stung as a child, right?

620
00:47:36.774 --> 00:47:40.244
Imagine a giant cockroach
with unlimited strength...

621
00:47:40.494 --> 00:47:43.930
...a massive inferiority complex,
and a real short temper...

622
00:47:44.134 --> 00:47:47.285
...is terrorizing Manhattan Island
in a new Edgar suit.

623
00:47:48.414 --> 00:47:49.483
That sound like fun?

624
00:47:51.814 --> 00:47:52.849
What's the move?

625
00:47:53.974 --> 00:47:56.329
With a bug in town,
we'll watch the morgues.

626
00:48:08.174 --> 00:48:09.926
Where do you want
contestant number 3?

627
00:48:10.134 --> 00:48:11.567
Just leave it there.

628
00:48:11.814 --> 00:48:12.849
What's with the cat?

629
00:48:13.094 --> 00:48:16.006
There's a problem with the cat.
Sign here.

630
00:48:16.254 --> 00:48:18.927
- What's the problem with the cat?
- It's your problem.

631
00:48:22.134 --> 00:48:23.613
I hate the living.

632
00:48:25.534 --> 00:48:26.853
Shall we?

633
00:48:55.294 --> 00:48:57.091
Oh, my God!

634
00:49:01.014 --> 00:49:02.925
Buddy, what are you?

635
00:49:10.974 --> 00:49:14.091
Subject was approximately 112 degrees
at time of autopsy...

636
00:49:14.334 --> 00:49:16.404
...indicating a temperature increase.

637
00:49:16.654 --> 00:49:20.613
Examiner tried to verify this rectally,
but the subject had no rectum.

638
00:49:20.854 --> 00:49:22.207
Which is really...

639
00:49:22.454 --> 00:49:23.284
Weird.

640
00:49:24.134 --> 00:49:28.127
I'm Dr. Leo Manville, Department
of Public Health. This is Dr. White.

641
00:49:29.134 --> 00:49:31.090
You must not have a home life.

642
00:49:31.294 --> 00:49:34.411
We watch the morgues carefully.
You have something unusual?

643
00:49:34.654 --> 00:49:36.849
I'd say so. Triple homicide.

644
00:49:37.094 --> 00:49:38.894
The first body was normal,
except he was broken in half.

645
00:49:38.894 --> 00:49:40.122
The first body was normal,
except he was broken in half.

646
00:49:40.374 --> 00:49:42.763
But when I opened up
the other two, well...

647
00:49:43.014 --> 00:49:43.924
Let me show you.

648
00:49:50.574 --> 00:49:53.566
There's a skeletal structure
unlike anything I've seen.

649
00:49:53.814 --> 00:49:55.213
I'll have a look at it.

650
00:49:55.414 --> 00:49:57.530
You and Dr. Weaver
check the other body.

651
00:49:57.734 --> 00:49:59.053
This way, doctor.

652
00:49:59.734 --> 00:50:01.531
This one's even stranger.

653
00:50:02.414 --> 00:50:04.974
I did a laparotomy.
I started with the stomach.

654
00:50:05.214 --> 00:50:08.524
But we can start with the
gastroesophageal junction.

655
00:50:09.614 --> 00:50:12.412
Let's start wherever you started at.

656
00:50:12.854 --> 00:50:14.128
Okey-dokey.

657
00:50:22.494 --> 00:50:24.007
- Is this your cat?
- It is now.

658
00:50:24.214 --> 00:50:26.489
It came in with the body.
Dive right in.

659
00:50:26.694 --> 00:50:28.332
I'm sure he won't mind.

660
00:50:31.814 --> 00:50:33.611
You have really pretty eyes.

661
00:50:34.574 --> 00:50:35.529
Thank you.

662
00:50:39.214 --> 00:50:40.090
Feel that?

663
00:50:40.294 --> 00:50:43.206
Where the pyloric junction would be?
Push it aside.

664
00:50:43.694 --> 00:50:46.572
Notice anything strange?
Stomach, liver, lungs...

665
00:50:46.974 --> 00:50:48.771
Nope, all fine.

666
00:50:49.014 --> 00:50:50.447
They're all missing.

667
00:50:51.174 --> 00:50:52.004
Of course.

668
00:50:52.254 --> 00:50:55.087
That's obviously
the first thing I noticed.

669
00:50:55.614 --> 00:50:58.492
What I was pointing out
is the fact that there are no...

670
00:50:59.614 --> 00:51:00.888
...pieces...

671
00:51:01.134 --> 00:51:02.567
...of them left.

672
00:51:02.814 --> 00:51:05.726
You know, so they're intact...

673
00:51:06.174 --> 00:51:09.166
...wherever they are whole.
That we can be sure of.

674
00:51:09.374 --> 00:51:10.727
Have we met before?

675
00:51:11.534 --> 00:51:13.525
I'm having a feeling of déjà vu.

676
00:51:14.974 --> 00:51:17.204
- Yeah, me too.
- Really?

677
00:51:17.974 --> 00:51:20.329
Wanna know what I think?
Don't tell him.

678
00:51:20.574 --> 00:51:23.771
He's under enough stress.
I don't think it's a real body.

679
00:51:24.014 --> 00:51:27.211
I think it's some kind of
transport unit for something else.

680
00:51:27.454 --> 00:51:29.206
The question is, what?

681
00:51:30.054 --> 00:51:31.533
Is this freaking you out?

682
00:51:34.414 --> 00:51:35.563
No, girl.

683
00:51:37.094 --> 00:51:39.927
You know what I like to do sometimes
when it's late?

684
00:51:44.094 --> 00:51:45.368
Dr. White.

685
00:51:47.054 --> 00:51:48.328
Excuse me.

686
00:51:52.854 --> 00:51:53.969
What do you think?

687
00:51:54.494 --> 00:51:57.566
Interesting. She got
a "Queen of the Undead" thing going...

688
00:51:57.814 --> 00:51:59.042
Of the body.

689
00:51:59.254 --> 00:52:00.050
Great body.

690
00:52:00.254 --> 00:52:01.892
The dead body.

691
00:52:02.654 --> 00:52:04.531
You have to look at that thing.

692
00:52:04.854 --> 00:52:06.207
You recognize him?

693
00:52:06.894 --> 00:52:10.250
He looks like the big guy I saw
at headquarters, only deader.

694
00:52:10.494 --> 00:52:11.768
What killed him?

695
00:52:13.014 --> 00:52:13.924
A bug?

696
00:52:14.774 --> 00:52:16.002
You're up, slugger.

697
00:52:19.894 --> 00:52:21.043
Look at this.

698
00:52:22.774 --> 00:52:24.127
What the hell is that?

699
00:52:41.934 --> 00:52:43.287
Must...

700
00:52:44.894 --> 00:52:46.771
To prevent...

701
00:52:49.134 --> 00:52:50.965
...contest.

702
00:52:51.974 --> 00:52:53.373
What are you saying?

703
00:52:53.614 --> 00:52:54.967
To prevent...

704
00:52:55.214 --> 00:52:56.647
To prevent...

705
00:52:56.934 --> 00:52:57.923
...struggle?

706
00:53:00.254 --> 00:53:01.243
To prevent...

707
00:53:01.774 --> 00:53:02.650
War?

708
00:53:03.014 --> 00:53:04.163
War.

709
00:53:06.654 --> 00:53:08.133
The Galaxy...

710
00:53:09.454 --> 00:53:11.126
...is on...

711
00:53:11.534 --> 00:53:13.365
...Orion's...

712
00:53:15.774 --> 00:53:16.570
...be...

713
00:53:19.374 --> 00:53:20.773
What is word?

714
00:53:21.374 --> 00:53:22.648
The bed?

715
00:53:23.134 --> 00:53:25.045
Belt? Orion's belt?

716
00:53:44.494 --> 00:53:47.725
"To prevent war, the Galaxy
is on Orion's belt."

717
00:53:47.974 --> 00:53:49.805
What the hell does that mean?

718
00:53:53.134 --> 00:53:54.567
Doctor...

719
00:53:54.774 --> 00:53:56.048
...whatever, come here.

720
00:53:56.294 --> 00:54:00.128
Dr. Whatever? You guys aren't really
from the Department of Health.

721
00:54:00.414 --> 00:54:02.166
Rosenberg. Damn!

722
00:54:02.414 --> 00:54:06.566
The Arquillians won't like this.
He was one of the royal family.

723
00:54:06.854 --> 00:54:08.003
This is an alien...

724
00:54:08.214 --> 00:54:11.411
...and you're from a government agency
keeping it under wraps.

725
00:54:11.614 --> 00:54:14.731
He said, "To prevent war,
the Galaxy is on Orion's belt."

726
00:54:14.974 --> 00:54:17.090
How else do you explain New York?

727
00:54:17.294 --> 00:54:19.569
I was in this cab, and this guy was...

728
00:54:21.374 --> 00:54:23.410
"Galaxy on Orion's belt"
makes no sense.

729
00:54:23.614 --> 00:54:27.402
That's what the little dude inside
the big dude's head said, right?

730
00:54:27.614 --> 00:54:30.447
Damn, man!
You did the flashy thing already.

731
00:54:30.694 --> 00:54:33.162
Whoever you are,
you'll have to show me I.D.

732
00:54:33.414 --> 00:54:36.326
Of course, young lady.
Look at this for me, please.

733
00:54:36.574 --> 00:54:38.326
- Would you stop that?
- What?

734
00:54:38.534 --> 00:54:40.570
That thing will give her brain cancer.

735
00:54:40.814 --> 00:54:42.964
Never hurt her before.
Close the doors.

736
00:54:43.214 --> 00:54:44.932
Special Services will be here.

737
00:54:45.174 --> 00:54:47.927
How many times have you
flashy-thinged that woman?

738
00:54:48.174 --> 00:54:48.970
Couple.

739
00:54:49.214 --> 00:54:52.331
- Don't you worry about long-term damage?
- A little.

740
00:54:52.574 --> 00:54:54.405
- Have you flashy-thinged me?
- No.

741
00:54:54.654 --> 00:54:57.009
I ain't playing with you! Have you?

742
00:55:06.254 --> 00:55:09.166
I think I should be in charge
of the flashy thing.

743
00:55:09.414 --> 00:55:10.767
Not while I'm around.

744
00:55:11.014 --> 00:55:13.130
You'll fricassee someone's brain.

745
00:55:13.374 --> 00:55:17.208
We got two dead aliens and
a medical examiner needs a new memory.

746
00:55:19.694 --> 00:55:21.924
Make it a happy memory.

747
00:55:53.814 --> 00:55:55.805
Where is it?!

748
00:56:37.814 --> 00:56:39.213
Hey, Zed.

749
00:56:39.734 --> 00:56:42.407
Doesn't anybody ever get
any sleep around here?

750
00:56:42.654 --> 00:56:46.408
The twins keep us on Centurian time.
It's a 37-hour day.

751
00:56:46.614 --> 00:56:48.764
Give it a few months.
You'll get used to it.

752
00:56:49.014 --> 00:56:50.572
Or have a psychotic episode.

753
00:56:51.054 --> 00:56:52.123
Here's Orion.

754
00:56:52.334 --> 00:56:55.212
It's a grouping of the brightest stars
in the northern sky.

755
00:56:55.454 --> 00:56:57.922
- Here's Orion's belt.
- The little guy said:

756
00:56:58.174 --> 00:57:01.371
"To prevent war, the Galaxy
is on Orion's belt."

757
00:57:01.614 --> 00:57:03.764
There are no galaxies
on Orion's belt.

758
00:57:04.014 --> 00:57:07.563
The belt is just these three stars.
Galaxies are huge.

759
00:57:07.774 --> 00:57:11.733
They're made up of billions of stars.
You heard wrong.

760
00:57:12.574 --> 00:57:14.929
Look, whatever, I know what I heard.

761
00:57:50.534 --> 00:57:51.808
Pretty lady.

762
00:57:58.014 --> 00:58:02.405
That grumpy guy's story's starting to
come into focus a little bit here.

763
00:58:03.094 --> 00:58:06.166
So you were the guy in that picture
with the flowers?

764
00:58:07.094 --> 00:58:10.291
And, I take it,
she never got those flowers.

765
00:58:10.974 --> 00:58:13.727
So, what, she ever get married
or anything?

766
00:58:14.894 --> 00:58:17.692
They say it's better to have
loved and lost...

767
00:58:17.894 --> 00:58:19.930
...than never to have loved at all.

768
00:58:20.174 --> 00:58:21.209
Try it.

769
00:58:26.654 --> 00:58:27.723
Look at this.

770
00:58:27.974 --> 00:58:29.373
They're all leaving.

771
00:58:29.614 --> 00:58:33.368
We've had 12 jumps in the last hour.
Redgick was just the first.

772
00:58:34.214 --> 00:58:35.932
What do they know that we don't?

773
00:58:36.174 --> 00:58:37.653
Why does a rat desert a ship?

774
00:58:37.854 --> 00:58:41.529
Give me Lem Sat 4, please,
with a proton induction thermoscan.

775
00:58:43.294 --> 00:58:45.444
Thank you. Okay. Lem Sat 18.

776
00:58:47.494 --> 00:58:48.643
All right, 4000.

777
00:58:52.854 --> 00:58:54.253
An Arquillian battle cruiser.

778
00:58:54.494 --> 00:58:57.054
And we've got
a dead Arquillian prince.

779
00:58:58.774 --> 00:59:00.207
Speak of the devil.

780
00:59:01.214 --> 00:59:02.090
They sound pissed.

781
00:59:02.334 --> 00:59:03.733
Translate that. Step on it.

782
00:59:04.094 --> 00:59:07.450
Go to Rosenberg's jewellery store,
and see what you can turn up.

783
00:59:13.174 --> 00:59:14.368
Give the kid a weapon.

784
00:59:23.814 --> 00:59:26.931
- Series 4 De-atomizer.
- That's what I'm talking about.

785
00:59:27.134 --> 00:59:28.726
Noisy Cricket.

786
00:59:30.774 --> 00:59:32.685
Kay, no, no, come on, man.

787
00:59:32.934 --> 00:59:35.289
You get a Series 4 De-atomizer...

788
00:59:35.534 --> 00:59:37.331
...I get a little midget Cricket?

789
00:59:41.174 --> 00:59:43.005
Feel like I'm gonna break it.

790
01:00:25.614 --> 01:00:27.809
Hey, this is my truck!

791
01:00:28.854 --> 01:00:31.846
Make sure you tell them that
down at the impound.

792
01:00:38.894 --> 01:00:40.771
Please.

793
01:00:49.814 --> 01:00:52.169
Who breaks into a jewellery store
and leaves the jewels?

794
01:00:52.414 --> 01:00:54.484
Somebody not looking for jewellery.

795
01:00:56.654 --> 01:00:59.009
This guy had a serious crush
on his cat.

796
01:01:01.534 --> 01:01:02.410
Get down!

797
01:01:07.534 --> 01:01:08.523
Man!

798
01:01:10.334 --> 01:01:12.165
That's him. That's the bug!

799
01:01:12.374 --> 01:01:13.693
In the Edgar suit!

800
01:01:34.494 --> 01:01:37.133
We do not discharge our weapons
in view of the public!

801
01:01:37.374 --> 01:01:39.251
We ain't got time for this bullshit!

802
01:01:39.494 --> 01:01:41.769
There's a alien battle cruiser
about to...

803
01:01:42.014 --> 01:01:44.767
There's always an alien battle
cruiser or a death ray...

804
01:01:45.014 --> 01:01:47.733
...or an intergalactic plague
about to wipe out life on Earth.

805
01:01:47.974 --> 01:01:50.772
The only way people get on
with their happy lives...

806
01:01:50.974 --> 01:01:53.568
...is they do not know about it!

807
01:01:58.134 --> 01:01:59.965
And don't worry about the bug.

808
01:02:00.254 --> 01:02:02.529
He's not leaving town.
We got his ship.

809
01:02:10.054 --> 01:02:11.965
We need a containment crew...

810
01:02:12.174 --> 01:02:13.766
<i>... on MacDougal Street. </i>

811
01:02:14.574 --> 01:02:18.044
Containment may be a moot point.
The exodus continues.

812
01:02:18.294 --> 01:02:21.969
The party's over, and the last one
to leave gets stuck with the check.

813
01:02:22.214 --> 01:02:24.569
You sorry little ingrates!

814
01:02:32.334 --> 01:02:33.926
<i>What about the Arquillians? </i>

815
01:02:34.174 --> 01:02:37.450
We've translated part of the message:
" Deliver the Galaxy."

816
01:02:37.694 --> 01:02:40.766
<i>-They don't want much, do they? </i>
- Oh, it gets better.

817
01:02:41.014 --> 01:02:42.413
They hold us responsible.

818
01:02:51.014 --> 01:02:52.925
Where do you keep your dead?

819
01:02:53.134 --> 01:02:54.852
I don't have any dead.

820
01:02:55.374 --> 01:02:56.409
Where?

821
01:02:56.654 --> 01:02:57.928
I don't know.

822
01:02:58.414 --> 01:03:00.325
The city morgue?

823
01:03:09.934 --> 01:03:12.243
That's three for a dollar, sir!

824
01:03:12.814 --> 01:03:15.647
It was some light
that refracted off of Venus...

825
01:03:15.894 --> 01:03:17.293
...into some swamp gas...

826
01:03:17.534 --> 01:03:18.967
...and that's what made the...

827
01:03:19.214 --> 01:03:20.567
All right, kid!

828
01:03:21.334 --> 01:03:22.687
Excuse me.
What's up?

829
01:03:22.934 --> 01:03:25.494
The Arquillians want the Galaxy,
whatever that means.

830
01:03:25.694 --> 01:03:27.446
We need help, a professional...

831
01:03:27.694 --> 01:03:30.731
...with years of experience
in intergalactic politics.

832
01:03:30.974 --> 01:03:33.534
I hope the little twerp
hasn't skipped town.

833
01:03:35.814 --> 01:03:37.566
If you'll gather over here...

834
01:03:37.814 --> 01:03:41.045
That's right, move in closer.
That's good. Thanks.

835
01:03:41.294 --> 01:03:44.604
If you look right here,
I'd appreciate it. Thank you.

836
01:03:57.134 --> 01:03:59.773
The worst disguise ever.
He's definitely an alien.

837
01:04:00.014 --> 01:04:02.687
You don't like it,
you can kiss my furry butt.

838
01:04:03.334 --> 01:04:04.164
Busy, Frank?

839
01:04:04.414 --> 01:04:06.450
Can't talk now.
My flight's leaving in...

840
01:04:06.694 --> 01:04:07.683
Get your paws off!

841
01:04:07.894 --> 01:04:09.043
Call the pound!

842
01:04:09.294 --> 01:04:11.285
The dog owes my friend money.

843
01:04:11.534 --> 01:04:13.047
Arquillians and bugs,
what do you know?

844
01:04:13.294 --> 01:04:14.488
- Nothing.
- Not a thing?

845
01:04:17.294 --> 01:04:19.728
Stop, stop, stop it!
Okay, okay!

846
01:04:20.094 --> 01:04:22.164
Rosenberg wasn't a two-bit Arquillian.

847
01:04:22.374 --> 01:04:25.571
He was the guardian of the Galaxy.
He thought he'd be safe on Earth.

848
01:04:25.814 --> 01:04:26.724
The bug had other plans.

849
01:04:26.934 --> 01:04:30.643
The Galaxy is the best source
for subatomic energy in the universe.

850
01:04:30.894 --> 01:04:33.533
If the bugs get it,
kiss the Arquillians goodbye.

851
01:04:33.774 --> 01:04:34.763
Ask about the belt.

852
01:04:35.014 --> 01:04:37.574
Rosenberg mentioned Orion's belt.
What did he mean?

853
01:04:37.814 --> 01:04:39.532
- Beats me.
- Beats you?

854
01:04:40.294 --> 01:04:41.409
Not around.

855
01:04:44.214 --> 01:04:46.170
It's a ventriloquist act.

856
01:04:46.414 --> 01:04:48.211
The Galaxy is here!

857
01:04:49.014 --> 01:04:49.810
Here?

858
01:04:50.014 --> 01:04:52.482
A galaxy's millions of stars
and planets.

859
01:04:52.734 --> 01:04:55.123
When will you learn
that size doesn't matter?

860
01:04:55.574 --> 01:04:58.486
If something's important,
it doesn't mean it's not small.

861
01:04:58.814 --> 01:04:59.769
How small?

862
01:04:59.974 --> 01:05:01.965
The size of a marble or a jewel.

863
01:05:02.454 --> 01:05:05.014
Excuse me. I gotta be walked
before my flight.

864
01:05:05.254 --> 01:05:06.084
Get out of here.

865
01:05:08.534 --> 01:05:11.765
If the Galaxy's here,
it's not on Orion's belt.

866
01:05:31.214 --> 01:05:33.170
When you want attention...

867
01:05:34.574 --> 01:05:35.370
Orion.

868
01:05:35.574 --> 01:05:37.246
That's a pretty name.

869
01:05:37.774 --> 01:05:39.253
What's this?

870
01:06:31.494 --> 01:06:33.530
Yes, good, thank you.

871
01:06:33.774 --> 01:06:36.732
Thank you for making sure
the bell works.

872
01:06:39.334 --> 01:06:40.972
What's up, Farmer John?

873
01:06:42.454 --> 01:06:44.922
A man came in here earlier.

874
01:06:45.494 --> 01:06:46.290
A dead man.

875
01:06:46.534 --> 01:06:48.411
And that means what to me?

876
01:06:50.374 --> 01:06:53.127
It was a very dear friend of mine.

877
01:06:53.814 --> 01:06:55.805
I believe he had an animal with him.

878
01:06:56.054 --> 01:06:58.488
It was a gift I gave him. A pet cat.

879
01:06:58.734 --> 01:07:00.292
It means worlds to me.

880
01:07:00.534 --> 01:07:02.206
I'd like to have it back.

881
01:07:02.454 --> 01:07:05.764
I'll need picture I.D.,
proof of ownership of the cat...

882
01:07:06.014 --> 01:07:09.370
...notarized proof of kinship
with the deceased.

883
01:07:10.294 --> 01:07:11.647
Don't do that.

884
01:07:13.334 --> 01:07:14.369
Do what?

885
01:07:15.494 --> 01:07:16.927
Don't do it.

886
01:07:19.414 --> 01:07:20.733
Oh, man.

887
01:07:35.774 --> 01:07:37.924
Look, Kay, let me handle this one.

888
01:07:38.174 --> 01:07:40.768
All we gotta do is get a cat.
It's not that hard.

889
01:07:41.014 --> 01:07:45.132
But if you go in there, you'll start
flashing your brain ray in her face.

890
01:07:45.334 --> 01:07:46.926
She'll wind up with leukemia.

891
01:07:47.174 --> 01:07:50.849
The doctor don't need you flashing away
her med-school classes. Five minutes.

892
01:07:51.094 --> 01:07:52.368
Two minutes.

893
01:07:54.774 --> 01:07:55.763
Where's the animal?

894
01:07:56.014 --> 01:07:57.413
I said I don't know.

895
01:07:57.614 --> 01:07:59.809
Well, let's see if we can find it.

896
01:08:05.014 --> 01:08:06.083
Hello!

897
01:08:14.974 --> 01:08:16.043
Hello!

898
01:08:20.294 --> 01:08:21.773
- How you doing?
- Hello.

899
01:08:22.014 --> 01:08:24.812
I'm Sergeant Friday
from the 26th Precinct.

900
01:08:25.054 --> 01:08:27.522
A cat came in with a corpse
the other day.

901
01:08:27.774 --> 01:08:29.765
- "Orion" on the nametag?
- Right.

902
01:08:30.574 --> 01:08:33.407
Well, this cat is a witness...

903
01:08:33.654 --> 01:08:36.009
...in a murder case.
I'll need to take him.

904
01:08:36.254 --> 01:08:37.767
I don't know where the cat is.

905
01:08:38.014 --> 01:08:39.242
You don't?

906
01:08:39.774 --> 01:08:42.368
No, but maybe you could take me
with you instead.

907
01:08:44.294 --> 01:08:47.172
Damn, you do start fast,
don't you?

908
01:08:47.374 --> 01:08:49.092
I'd really like to go with you...

909
01:08:49.414 --> 01:08:50.369
...now.

910
01:08:51.294 --> 01:08:53.569
And exactly why is that?

911
01:09:00.574 --> 01:09:02.485
I need to show you something.

912
01:09:03.054 --> 01:09:03.964
Slow down.

913
01:09:04.214 --> 01:09:07.331
- Girl, don't hit the gas like that!
- You don't understand.

914
01:09:07.574 --> 01:09:09.724
You really need to see this.

915
01:09:09.974 --> 01:09:14.365
I will. One thing. I gotta drive.
It's not some macho trip.

916
01:09:14.574 --> 01:09:16.883
That's just the way I get down.

917
01:09:27.574 --> 01:09:30.088
Look, stud, you're
really not getting this.

918
01:09:30.294 --> 01:09:33.286
There's something I need you
to help me with.

919
01:09:43.774 --> 01:09:44.809
Freeze it!

920
01:09:45.054 --> 01:09:46.043
You are thick!

921
01:09:46.294 --> 01:09:47.363
How could I know?

922
01:09:47.574 --> 01:09:48.768
Did I have to sing it?

923
01:09:49.014 --> 01:09:50.493
You were like a drunk prom date.

924
01:09:50.734 --> 01:09:54.443
Typical. Anytime a woman shows
even a hint of sexual independence...

925
01:09:54.654 --> 01:09:55.450
Shut up!

926
01:09:55.654 --> 01:09:56.450
Let her go!

927
01:09:56.654 --> 01:09:58.372
Listen, monkey-boy...

928
01:09:58.614 --> 01:10:01.686
...l'm on the top rung
of the evolutionary ladder.

929
01:10:01.934 --> 01:10:02.969
So can it.

930
01:10:03.214 --> 01:10:05.603
Show me your face,
and I'll cure your ills.

931
01:10:05.894 --> 01:10:09.125
Ever pull wings off a fly?
Care to see the fly get even?

932
01:10:09.334 --> 01:10:10.687
What about your ship?

933
01:10:10.934 --> 01:10:13.732
If that's what you call
that trash we got locked up.

934
01:10:13.974 --> 01:10:16.249
- Put your weapons down!
- Won't happen.

935
01:10:16.494 --> 01:10:17.290
It's okay.

936
01:10:17.574 --> 01:10:19.053
How is it okay?

937
01:10:19.294 --> 01:10:21.285
I'm saying it's gonna be okay.

938
01:10:21.534 --> 01:10:23.365
Don't bet on it, meat sack.

939
01:10:32.734 --> 01:10:34.213
Let me go!

940
01:10:44.734 --> 01:10:45.928
Go on!

941
01:10:49.774 --> 01:10:51.002
Take me here.

942
01:10:51.254 --> 01:10:52.050
No way.

943
01:10:53.454 --> 01:10:54.250
Take me!

944
01:11:11.574 --> 01:11:12.370
He's in a cab!

945
01:11:33.934 --> 01:11:36.209
Don't move! Don't move!
Don't move!

946
01:11:36.734 --> 01:11:38.133
Hey, man, what?

947
01:11:48.934 --> 01:11:51.653
He's not leaving the planet in a cab.
Let's go.

948
01:11:56.414 --> 01:11:58.974
Put up a bionet
all the way around Manhattan.

949
01:11:59.214 --> 01:12:01.409
If it's not human, it doesn't leave.

950
01:12:02.734 --> 01:12:04.247
What do we hear from upstairs?

951
01:12:04.494 --> 01:12:05.643
" Deliver the Galaxy."

952
01:12:05.894 --> 01:12:08.772
The bug's got the Galaxy,
but we got his ship.

953
01:12:11.814 --> 01:12:14.044
<i>Warning: </i>
<i>Plutonic fusion detection. </i>

954
01:12:15.094 --> 01:12:17.369
<i>Warning: </i>
<i>Plutonic fusion detection. </i>

955
01:12:21.854 --> 01:12:24.288
- Why are they shooting at us?
- Battle rules.

956
01:12:24.534 --> 01:12:28.607
We get an ultimatum, a warning shot,
then a galactic week to respond.

957
01:12:29.174 --> 01:12:31.608
A galactic week?
How the hell long is that?

958
01:12:31.854 --> 01:12:32.889
One hour.

959
01:12:33.254 --> 01:12:34.369
One hour?

960
01:12:34.894 --> 01:12:35.929
Then what?

961
01:12:41.054 --> 01:12:42.203
That's bullshit!

962
01:12:42.414 --> 01:12:46.202
To keep the bugs from getting it,
Arquillians will destroy that galaxy.

963
01:12:46.454 --> 01:12:48.843
And whatever planet it's on.

964
01:12:49.934 --> 01:12:51.333
You're talking about us.

965
01:12:51.574 --> 01:12:52.927
Sucks, huh?

966
01:12:55.414 --> 01:12:58.053
I'll get the location
of every interstellar vehicle.

967
01:12:58.294 --> 01:13:00.364
I already did.
Frank took the last ship.

968
01:13:00.614 --> 01:13:02.684
- Sneden's Landing and Throg's Neck.
- Gone.

969
01:13:02.934 --> 01:13:04.652
- What about Atlantic City?
- Gone.

970
01:13:04.894 --> 01:13:06.247
- Bayonne?
- Gone.

971
01:13:06.494 --> 01:13:08.928
- There's Three Mile Island.
- Gone.

972
01:13:09.174 --> 01:13:11.165
- Staten Island?
- Gone, thank God.

973
01:13:11.574 --> 01:13:15.283
We're running out of time. If that
bug gets off Earth, we're bug food.

974
01:13:15.534 --> 01:13:16.569
Hey, old guys!

975
01:13:21.454 --> 01:13:23.251
Do those still work?

976
01:13:37.854 --> 01:13:39.810
- You're coming with me.
- What?

977
01:13:40.334 --> 01:13:42.134
It's a long trip.
I'll need a snack.

978
01:13:42.134 --> 01:13:43.089
It's a long trip.
I'll need a snack.

979
01:13:48.854 --> 01:13:49.764
The tunnel?

980
01:13:50.014 --> 01:13:52.767
- You know a better way to Queens?
- It'll be packed!

981
01:14:05.654 --> 01:14:06.882
Remember the red button?

982
01:14:07.494 --> 01:14:09.086
Push the red button.

983
01:14:09.854 --> 01:14:11.128
Put on a seat belt.

984
01:14:23.174 --> 01:14:25.688
You're much too tense.
You're young. Relax.

985
01:14:25.934 --> 01:14:27.606
Take some joy in your work.

986
01:14:27.854 --> 01:14:28.969
Do you like music?

987
01:14:32.974 --> 01:14:33.963
That's better.

988
01:14:34.174 --> 01:14:37.484
<i>... in Norfolk, Virginia</i>
<i>California on my mind</i>

989
01:14:37.934 --> 01:14:40.494
<i>I straddled that Greyhound</i>
<i>And rode him into Raleigh</i>

990
01:14:40.694 --> 01:14:42.412
<i>And on across Caroline</i>

991
01:14:42.814 --> 01:14:45.647
<i>Somebody help me</i>
<i>Get out of Louisiana</i>

992
01:14:47.534 --> 01:14:49.809
<i>There are people there</i>
<i>Who care a little 'bout me</i>

993
01:14:50.014 --> 01:14:53.245
<i>-And won't let the poor boy down</i>
- All right, now!

994
01:15:04.334 --> 01:15:05.847
You do know Elvis is dead?

995
01:15:06.094 --> 01:15:08.528
No, Elvis is not dead.
He just went home.

996
01:15:23.254 --> 01:15:24.733
You don't wanna eat me.

997
01:15:24.974 --> 01:15:27.647
I'm an important person on my planet.
Like a queen!

998
01:15:27.854 --> 01:15:30.573
A goddess, even.
There are those who worship me.

999
01:15:30.814 --> 01:15:32.486
I'm not trying to impress you.

1000
01:15:32.734 --> 01:15:34.690
I'm just saying it could start a war!

1001
01:15:34.934 --> 01:15:37.368
Good, war. That means
more food for my family.

1002
01:15:37.614 --> 01:15:40.845
All 78 million of them.
That's a lot of mouths to feed.

1003
01:15:41.054 --> 01:15:43.568
You're a wonderful dad,
but I'm staying here!

1004
01:16:04.334 --> 01:16:06.370
Now, that's what I'm talking about.

1005
01:16:07.614 --> 01:16:09.366
Roaches check in.

1006
01:16:11.334 --> 01:16:12.528
They don't check out.

1007
01:16:17.134 --> 01:16:21.013
<i>Warning: E ight minutes</i>
<i>to the destruction of Earth. </i>

1008
01:16:22.734 --> 01:16:23.962
<i>E ight minutes... </i>

1009
01:16:24.214 --> 01:16:25.408
<i>... to destruction. </i>

1010
01:17:08.774 --> 01:17:11.493
We'll use pulsar level five
with an implosion factor.

1011
01:17:11.734 --> 01:17:12.530
What?!

1012
01:17:12.734 --> 01:17:15.806
Just shoot the damn thing
on the count of three. One...

1013
01:17:16.054 --> 01:17:17.203
...two, three!

1014
01:18:15.454 --> 01:18:16.967
You idiots!

1015
01:18:18.174 --> 01:18:19.892
You don't get it!

1016
01:18:20.134 --> 01:18:20.964
I've won.

1017
01:18:21.774 --> 01:18:21.974
It's over.

1018
01:18:21.974 --> 01:18:23.487
It's over.

1019
01:18:23.934 --> 01:18:25.765
You're milk-suckers!

1020
01:18:26.374 --> 01:18:27.966
You don't matter.

1021
01:18:28.254 --> 01:18:30.609
In a few seconds,
you won't even be matter.

1022
01:18:30.854 --> 01:18:33.448
You're under arrest
for violating the Tycho Treaty.

1023
01:18:33.694 --> 01:18:36.333
So hand over whatever galaxy
you might be carrying...

1024
01:18:36.574 --> 01:18:39.168
...and put your hands on your head.

1025
01:18:43.974 --> 01:18:45.726
I'll put my hands...

1026
01:18:48.134 --> 01:18:49.328
...on my head.

1027
01:18:53.574 --> 01:18:54.529
Like this?

1028
01:19:22.654 --> 01:19:24.645
That did not go the way I planned.

1029
01:19:24.894 --> 01:19:26.486
Don't let him on the second ship.

1030
01:19:26.734 --> 01:19:29.532
- What are you talking about?
- Keep him on this planet.

1031
01:19:29.774 --> 01:19:31.651
Where are you going?

1032
01:19:32.254 --> 01:19:34.051
I'm gonna get my gun back.

1033
01:19:36.734 --> 01:19:37.530
Hey, bug!

1034
01:19:37.774 --> 01:19:40.572
You know how many of your kind
I've swatted with a paper?

1035
01:19:40.814 --> 01:19:43.203
You're just a smear
on the sports page...

1036
01:19:43.454 --> 01:19:46.252
...you slimy, gut-sucking,
intestinal parasite!

1037
01:19:46.734 --> 01:19:48.087
Eat me!

1038
01:19:48.294 --> 01:19:49.568
Eat me!

1039
01:20:07.134 --> 01:20:08.010
What's up?

1040
01:20:08.574 --> 01:20:11.646
You just gonna eat and run?
What about dessert?

1041
01:20:17.374 --> 01:20:18.727
That's it?

1042
01:20:19.134 --> 01:20:22.444
Where you going?
This party's just getting started.

1043
01:20:23.174 --> 01:20:24.448
Where you going?

1044
01:20:25.414 --> 01:20:27.052
Where you going?

1045
01:20:28.174 --> 01:20:29.209
Let me tell you.

1046
01:20:29.454 --> 01:20:32.764
There's only one way off this planet,
and that's through me.

1047
01:21:14.534 --> 01:21:15.933
Where you going?

1048
01:21:16.774 --> 01:21:18.207
Why you running, huh?

1049
01:21:18.654 --> 01:21:20.292
I'm still standing.

1050
01:21:20.934 --> 01:21:22.845
Come on, bring it. Bring it!

1051
01:21:41.894 --> 01:21:44.249
I'm sorry.
Was that your auntie?

1052
01:21:46.374 --> 01:21:48.126
That means that's your uncle.

1053
01:21:51.014 --> 01:21:52.208
You all look alike.

1054
01:22:00.254 --> 01:22:01.972
Well, well.

1055
01:22:02.214 --> 01:22:05.570
Big, bad bug got
a bit of a soft spot, huh?

1056
01:22:09.094 --> 01:22:11.085
I can't understand why you gotta...

1057
01:22:11.334 --> 01:22:13.689
...come down here
bringing all this ruckus...

1058
01:22:13.934 --> 01:22:16.573
...snatching up galaxies
and everything.

1059
01:22:16.774 --> 01:22:20.733
My attitude is, don't start nothing,
won't be nothing.

1060
01:22:26.734 --> 01:22:30.249
Ease up out of my face before
something bad happens to you.

1061
01:22:32.254 --> 01:22:33.289
Too late.

1062
01:23:01.774 --> 01:23:04.083
Tell the Arquillians
we have the Galaxy.

1063
01:23:04.334 --> 01:23:06.052
<i>You got it, friend. </i>

1064
01:23:07.654 --> 01:23:09.690
Going to get your gun back, huh?

1065
01:23:09.934 --> 01:23:11.333
I like this gun.

1066
01:23:12.054 --> 01:23:16.093
While you was in there playing around,
I was doing all the work.

1067
01:23:16.334 --> 01:23:19.167
I had to bean him in the head
with this big rock.

1068
01:23:19.414 --> 01:23:21.245
I was gonna hit him with a 2-by-4.

1069
01:23:21.494 --> 01:23:23.007
He kicked me. It hurt.

1070
01:23:23.254 --> 01:23:25.893
But then I got to the fire.
I was like that with it.

1071
01:23:26.134 --> 01:23:28.443
Not bad for your second
day of work, is it?

1072
01:23:29.254 --> 01:23:32.451
This definitely rates a 9.0
on my weird-shit-o-metre.

1073
01:23:32.854 --> 01:23:36.449
Should've been here for
the Zeronion migration in 1968.

1074
01:23:38.974 --> 01:23:41.488
I guess you weren't even alive in '68.

1075
01:23:46.934 --> 01:23:49.448
Interesting job you guys have.

1076
01:24:04.934 --> 01:24:06.686
I know we got these rules...

1077
01:24:06.934 --> 01:24:09.084
...but she did help us bust that bug.

1078
01:24:09.334 --> 01:24:11.894
Maybe we didn't have to
flashy-thing her.

1079
01:24:13.494 --> 01:24:16.566
Come on. Who will she tell?
She hang out with dead people.

1080
01:24:16.814 --> 01:24:18.372
It's not for her.

1081
01:24:18.614 --> 01:24:19.842
It's for me.

1082
01:24:21.494 --> 01:24:22.768
What?

1083
01:24:24.894 --> 01:24:26.043
Aren't they beautiful?

1084
01:24:27.774 --> 01:24:28.570
Stars.

1085
01:24:29.174 --> 01:24:32.086
I never look at them anymore,
but they actually are...

1086
01:24:34.734 --> 01:24:36.053
...beautiful.

1087
01:24:40.534 --> 01:24:42.809
Kay, you're frightening your partner.

1088
01:24:43.054 --> 01:24:46.046
I've been training a replacement,
not a partner.

1089
01:24:47.054 --> 01:24:48.612
Wait a minute, Kay.

1090
01:24:49.094 --> 01:24:51.244
I cannot do this job by myself.

1091
01:24:51.494 --> 01:24:54.054
Guys, my apartment isn't
anywhere near here.

1092
01:24:54.254 --> 01:24:56.131
It's not even on the same island.

1093
01:24:57.654 --> 01:24:58.609
Days...

1094
01:24:58.814 --> 01:24:59.963
...months...

1095
01:25:00.214 --> 01:25:01.329
...years.

1096
01:25:01.654 --> 01:25:03.246
Always face it forward.

1097
01:25:12.534 --> 01:25:15.094
I was in an interstellar
cockroach's gullet.

1098
01:25:15.334 --> 01:25:17.643
That's one of 100 memories
I don't want.

1099
01:25:34.054 --> 01:25:35.328
See you around.

1100
01:25:41.334 --> 01:25:42.449
No...

1101
01:25:43.214 --> 01:25:44.442
...you won't.

1102
01:26:18.894 --> 01:26:21.010
The high consulate
from Solaxium 9...

1103
01:26:21.214 --> 01:26:23.045
...wants seats for the Bulls game.

1104
01:26:23.294 --> 01:26:25.762
Call Dennis Rodman.
He's from that planet.

1105
01:26:27.934 --> 01:26:29.492
Rodman? You're kidding.

1106
01:26:29.774 --> 01:26:30.763
Nope.

1107
01:26:31.334 --> 01:26:33.290
Not much of a disguise.
